{"title":"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(similar_to_Solution_1,_but_with_more_detail)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (similar to Solution 1, but with more detail)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21e377326f7511ad9dee19131d06d62b89345838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = \\sum_{k = 1}^{100} \\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"171\" height=\"50\" />. Find the largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0e44cd7a252c8d5021415ed12cfe3a1ffd23c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) \\le 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly increasing in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We realize that we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> terms to add up to around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, so we need some sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s, and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s.\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4dac3fb66ba092b186ba4b43de3d86d9dd081a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\approx 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> (alternatively, use binary search to get to this, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5319d202d65689eb59e7b154df65bcb90fe6fa79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\le 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />). Manually checking shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877d6b6409f5a1f3bb2f3e0649f24110b05c15c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(109) = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e085c33ea5e9daf5027a621e48e89ece9b266ecf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(110) &gt; 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/29116fd0da8cf9c424e6bbbcd6477e9b155d7453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{109}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because we want the value for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124f67db7a6afa865c501ba50ab4b611cbc8af28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, the average value of the 100 terms of the sequence should be around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d533d4d05845bf6285c0b1734c8264bc8cc1632e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/9253c953a94f7f21fba532d029a0be2c65d2e7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 \\le kn &lt; 10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />. We want kn to be around the middle of that range, and for k to be in the middle of 0 and 100, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/eccbb2e52f244126afa4c45c775b0cbe26bcef00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=50$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf48fec7cf376d86c71a22738538d51fb132ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50n=\\frac{10000+1000}{2}=\\frac{11000}{2}=5500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"295\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/713f2d87c3760c399f1d0a6b89dbace253b2834e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 110$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df61154236b47f3f3afdb74945734519b5c83d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(110) = 301$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, so we want to lower <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4c37ff1a89a2667cb70c3e6e731b7040a36bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$109$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, so our answer is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/29116fd0da8cf9c424e6bbbcd6477e9b155d7453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{109}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> where the sum is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, all the terms in the sum must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of terms less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of terms equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (also counted in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />). With this definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> the total will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34834e9be225d25e2e4b0ef783c549949d40dcb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 - M - N \\le 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"15\" />, from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac300647bd64e8908ed15b63940355854babb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M + N \\ge 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />. Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe144e5517842d0ce8986c6fada40267e99bd6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> is the smallest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f44ada375de9dbc2b35462089bb77d1a7899ef65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}(kn) \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae679eb5c037371734da222c94c431f71b296b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kn \\ge 10000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/40394b482cc9cfd8d29cfbf3e7ca69676d62b09a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M = \\left\\lfloor\\frac{9999}{n}\\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"43\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b875119a13fb8de1cc78c8412a3cb2304df021.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = \\left\\lfloor\\frac{999}{n}\\right\\rfloor = \\left\\lfloor\\frac{M}{10}\\right\\rfloor.\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae32cc20a44b1a625c2549d6a477e460e5f48f4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{M}{10} \\right\\rfloor \\ge 100 \\implies M \\ge \\left\\lceil\\frac{1000}{11}\\right\\rceil = 91 \\implies n \\le \\left\\lfloor\\frac{9999}{91}\\right\\rfloor = 109.\\]\" width=\"534\" height=\"43\" /> Since we want the largest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the answer is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/29116fd0da8cf9c424e6bbbcd6477e9b155d7453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{109}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28similar_to_Solution_1.2C_but_with_more_detail.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(similar_to_Solution_1,_but_with_more_detail)\">Solution 4 (similar to Solution 1, but with more detail)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (similar to Solution 1, but with more detail)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we're working with base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> logarithms, we can start by testing out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />'s that are powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the terms in the sum are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a24cee58b75d3764095181ab63a87340c64277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (1)\\rfloor, \\lfloor \\log_{10} (2)\\rfloor, \\lfloor \\log_{10} (3) \\rfloor , . . . , \\lfloor \\log_{10} (100) \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"370\" height=\"19\" />. For numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f5425f7b477bfb33193cd74af81b91942f5527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. Then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfa7b207fd044b8fd3e789137e2df1ee1135ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. The last number we have is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee173d62c561702fa2e0ebf8a61b512e60b3466e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. This sum gives us only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68267c4144972cd8f32261dbec69cc7bd1def4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 + 2 = 92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, which is much too low. However, applying the same counting technique for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa17013a449147f7545eaf8c6efd44b5b9fa2034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, our sum comes out to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c97d0ba5fea61373a1407ad60f4ae1cc50b6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 180 + 3 = 192$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />, since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfa7b207fd044b8fd3e789137e2df1ee1135ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee173d62c561702fa2e0ebf8a61b512e60b3466e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />, and one term for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/0/7c03bca42785d9f612d777764c363046e28fb595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\log_{10} (kn) \\rfloor = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />. So we go up one more power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/6084dd0ae591779d1e02cbc56bcc04c1d9303829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 270 + 4 = 292$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />, which is very close to what we are looking for. \n</p><p>Now we only have to bump up the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> a bit and check our sum. Each increase in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> actually increases the value of our sum by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as well (except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28f330a30091315e4652d36a5865a65c8f5dcb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />), because whenever a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is added to the sum, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is taken away. It doesn't take long to check and see that the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> we're looking for is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/29116fd0da8cf9c424e6bbbcd6477e9b155d7453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{109}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> , which corresponds to a sum of exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~ anellipticcurveoverq\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7uBkuNc4Gdg?si=f4gu7_JA1pODQUY0\">2010 AIME I #14</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I\" title=\"2010 AIME I\">2010 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2010\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175946\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 528/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1790/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 112/2097152 bytes\nHi